  "name": "TOTAL EOSINOPHIL COUNT",
  "code": "1589",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"58\" data-end=\"90\">Total Eosinophil Count (TEC)</strong> measures the number of <strong data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"129\">eosinophils</strong>, a type of white blood cell, in peripheral blood. Eosinophils play a role in <strong data-start=\"207\" data-end=\"229\">allergic reactions</strong>, <strong data-start=\"231\" data-end=\"255\">parasitic infections</strong>, and certain <strong data-start=\"269\" data-end=\"306\">immune or inflammatory conditions</strong>.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Eosinophil Count</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;500 cells/&mu;L</strong></td>\n<td>Mild eosinophilia</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;1500 cells/&mu;L</strong></td>\n<td>Moderate to severe eosinophilia</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;5000 cells/&mu;L</strong></td>\n<td>Hypereosinophilia (may cause tissue damage)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"931\"><strong data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"931\">Possible Causes of Eosinophilia:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"932\" data-end=\"1316\">\n<li data-start=\"932\" data-end=\"981\">\n<p data-start=\"934\" data-end=\"981\"><strong data-start=\"934\" data-end=\"958\">Parasitic infections</strong> (especially helminths)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"982\" data-end=\"1035\">\n<p data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1035\"><strong data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1007\">Allergic conditions</strong> (asthma, hay fever, eczema)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1036\" data-end=\"1115\">\n<p data-start=\"1038\" data-end=\"1115\"><strong data-start=\"1038\" data-end=\"1061\">Autoimmune diseases</strong> (e.g., eosinophilic granulomatosis with polyangiitis)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1166\">\n<p data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1166\"><strong data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1136\">Skin disorders</strong> (e.g., dermatitis, pemphigus)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1194\">\n<p data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1194\"><strong data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1194\">Drug hypersensitivity</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1195\" data-end=\"1266\">\n<p data-start=\"1197\" data-end=\"1266\"><strong data-start=\"1197\" data-end=\"1216\">Certain cancers</strong> (e.g., Hodgkin&rsquo;s lymphoma, eosinophilic leukemia)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1267\" data-end=\"1316\">\n<p data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1316\"><strong data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1316\">Idiopathic hypereosinophilic syndrome (HES)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1365\"><strong data-start=\"1328\" data-end=\"1365\">Low or Normal Eosinophil Count</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1366\" data-end=\"1564\">\n<li data-start=\"1366\" data-end=\"1425\">\n<p data-start=\"1368\" data-end=\"1425\"><strong data-start=\"1368\" data-end=\"1384\">&lt;40 cells/&mu;L</strong> is generally not clinically significant.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1426\" data-end=\"1564\">\n<p data-start=\"1428\" data-end=\"1470\"><strong data-start=\"1428\" data-end=\"1454\">Suppressed eosinophils</strong> may be seen in:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1473\" data-end=\"1564\">\n<li data-start=\"1473\" data-end=\"1509\">\n<p data-start=\"1475\" data-end=\"1509\">Acute stress or corticosteroid use</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1564\">\n<p data-start=\"1514\" data-end=\"1564\">Certain infections (especially bacterial or viral)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1600\"><strong data-start=\"1575\" data-end=\"1600\">Clinical Significance</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1601\" data-end=\"1867\">\n<li data-start=\"1601\" data-end=\"1649\">\n<p data-start=\"1603\" data-end=\"1649\">Mild eosinophilia may be transient and benign.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1650\" data-end=\"1778\">\n<p data-start=\"1652\" data-end=\"1778\">Persistent or high eosinophilia should prompt evaluation for underlying causes, especially parasitic or hematologic disorders.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1779\" data-end=\"1867\">\n<p data-start=\"1781\" data-end=\"1867\">If very high, risk of <strong data-start=\"1803\" data-end=\"1824\">organ involvement</strong> (lungs, heart, GI tract) must be assessed.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
